<title>CHILE: CTC 1996 earnings up 30 percent on 1995.</title>
<headline>CTC 1996 earnings up 30 percent on 1995.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's largest telecom Compania de Telecomunicaciones de Chile said net earnings rose 30 percent last year to 150.5 billion pesos compared with 116.2 billion pesos in 1995.</p>
<p>The company reported operating profits increasing to 136 billion pesos from 113.7 billion pesos in 1995.</p>
<p>Non-operating earnings climbed to 22.3 billion pesos from 2.9 billion pesos in the previous year.</p>
<p>The firm's long-distance unit CTC Mundo reported net earnings soaring to 9.7 billion pesos from 158.7 million pesos in 1995.</p>
</text>
